## 6. Success Criteria

| Scenario | Expected Behaviour |
|---|---|
| Advisor recommends averaging down, trade not executed | Narrative updated with market context only; no avg cost or stop-loss written; portfolio block unchanged and authoritative next run |
| Advisor recommends exit, trade not executed | Narrative updated with market reasoning only; no "position exited" written; portfolio block remains the record |
| Narrative and portfolio block conflict on cost basis | Advisor detects conflict, flags it, uses portfolio block, corrects narrative |
| Narrative references analyst price target | Allowed — this is market data, not portfolio state |
| Narrative references stock trading near a support level | Allowed — external market price, not personal cost basis |
| Narrative references "our stop-loss at $166.68" | Not allowed — stop-loss derives from cost basis, belongs in portfolio block |

---

## 7. What Does Not Change

- Narrative structure (add / update / resolve) — unchanged
- Narrative themes and categories — unchanged
- Portfolio data block format and content — unchanged
- All reasoning frameworks — unchanged
- Response JSON format — unchanged
- This is a prompt instruction change only — no application code changes required

---

## 8. Out of Scope

- This CR does not define how the portfolio block is generated or updated from trade records — that is a system concern outside the prompt
- This CR does not add trade confirmation tracking to the CLI
- This CR does not change how narratives are stored or retrieved between runs